    "proved": "Distinct normalized ordinary models have identical zero singularity volumes and the same ideal model. This holds in positive closed projective backgrounds in every dimension at least two, and genuinely nonclosed positive backgrounds with bounded mass in every dimension at least three. Top-volume comparison fails to separate them.",
    "mechanism": "Lift a normalized diffuse polar curve model through the divisorial product envelope identity. For the nonclosed case, a varying positive coefficient on a second curve factor retains the first-factor ordinary model by restriction to every horizontal section; submersion pullback gives trivial ideals. A further divisor factor forces every ordinary representative to have zero extended top-degree mass. A dominating closed product metric supplies bounded mass.",
    "retained_boundary": "No converse at general zero ideal volume, no ideal-theoretic positivity criterion, no dimension-two nonclosed example and no complete higher-dimensional model topology are asserted."
